      "hints": [
        "Expand $T_4 = \\binom{5}{3}(2x)^2\\left(-\\frac{1}{2x}\\right)^3 = -\\frac{5}{x}$.",
        "Expand $T_5 = \\binom{5}{4}(2x)\\left(-\\frac{1}{2x}\\right)^4 = \\frac{5}{8x^3}$.",
        "Expand $T_6 = \\binom{5}{5}\\left(-\\frac{1}{2x}\\right)^5 = -\\frac{1}{32x^5}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Calculate the 4th, 5th, and 6th terms of the binomial expansion of $\\left(2x - \\frac{1}{2x}\\right)^5$:\n$$T_4 = \\binom{5}{3}(2x)^2\\left(-\\frac{1}{2x}\\right)^3 = 10(4x^2)\\left(-\\frac{1}{8x^3}\\right) = -\\frac{5}{x}$$\n$$T_5 = \\binom{5}{4}(2x)^1\\left(-\\frac{1}{2x}\\right)^4 = 5(2x)\\left(\\frac{1}{16x^4}\\right) = \\frac{5}{8x^3}$$\n$$T_6 = \\binom{5}{5}\\left(-\\frac{1}{2x}\\right)^5 = 1\\left(-\\frac{1}{32x^5}\\right) = -\\frac{1}{32x^5}$$",
        "State the remaining three terms:\n$$-\\frac{5}{x} + \\frac{5}{8x^3} - \\frac{1}{32x^5} \\quad \\left(\\text{or } -5x^{-1} + \\frac{5}{8}x^{-3} - \\frac{1}{32}x^{-5}\\right)$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
